  <!-- 5-STEP CONTRIBUTOR GUIDE -->
  <section class="onboarding" id="guide">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="guide.badge">Onboarding Fast-Track</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="guide.title">Start Contributing in 5 Steps</h2>
        <p data-i18n="guide.subtitle">From zero to your first merged pull request. Here is how to get your development environment running in minutes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="quickstart-steps">
        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">1</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s1_title">1. Fork &amp; Clone Repositories</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s1_desc">Fork any Krewire repository to your personal GitHub account, then clone it locally to begin:</p>
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/your-username/krewire
cd krewire</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">2</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s2_title">2. Initialize Workspace (go.work)</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s2_desc">If working across multiple repos, synchronize your local Go workspace seamlessly with Go 1.27.1+:</p>
          <pre><code>go work init ./krewire ./mdbind
go work use ./krewire ./mdbind</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">3</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s3_title">3. Pick an Open Issue</h3>
          <p data-i18n-html="guide.s3_desc_html">Browse our curated issues list tagged with <span class="tag-issue">good-first-issue</span> or <span class="tag-issue">help-wanted</span>. Comment to let maintainers know you are working on it.</p>
          <div class="mt-4">
            <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3Agood-first-issue" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" data-i18n="guide.s3_btn">View Good First Issues →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">4</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s4_title">4. Implement &amp; Verify Locally</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s4_desc">Write clean, idiomatic Go code and tests. Verify that all 3 Quality Gates pass with zero failures:</p>
          <pre><code>gofmt -l .
go vet ./...
go test -race ./...</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="qs-card">
          <div class="qs-num">5</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="guide.s5_title">5. Submit PR with Conventional Commits</h3>
          <p data-i18n="guide.s5_desc">Open a PR following Conventional Commits (feat, fix, docs, refactor, test). Maintainers and AI Boost will review and guide you to merge.</p>
          <pre><code>git checkout -b feat/my-feature
git commit -m "feat(web): add handler (ref #123)"
git push origin feat/my-feature</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 AUTOMATED QUALITY GATES -->
  <section class="standards" id="standards">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="standards.badge">Quality Assurance</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="standards.title">The Krewire Way: 3 Quality Gates</h2>
        <p data-i18n="standards.subtitle">To keep the codebase reliable, predictable, and production-ready, every pull request passes through three automated gates.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="gates-grid">
        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">✓</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate1_title">Gate 1: Format &amp; Lint</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate1_desc">Zero lint errors and idiomatic Go formatting. Code must adhere strictly to Go standard conventions.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate1_req">Required: gofmt -l . (clean), go vet ./... (clean)</div>
        </div>

        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">🛡️</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate2_title">Gate 2: Race &amp; Tests</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate2_desc">Every commit is verified with race condition detection and comprehensive unit &amp; integration tests.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate2_req">Required: 100% test pass, 0 data races</div>
        </div>

        <div class="gate-card">
          <div class="gate-icon">📝</div>
          <h3 data-i18n="standards.gate3_title">Gate 3: Spec &amp; Commits</h3>
          <p data-i18n="standards.gate3_desc">Changes must link to a valid Spec or Issue, following Conventional Commits format.</p>
          <div class="gate-req" data-i18n="standards.gate3_req">Required: Semantic commit format &amp; spec traceability</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPONSORSHIP & OPEN CORE MODEL HUB -->
  <section class="sponsorship-section" id="sponsorship">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head w-full text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="sponsorship.badge">Open Core Model</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="sponsorship.title">The Four-Rung Tier Ladder &amp; Sponsorship</h2>
        <p data-i18n="sponsorship.subtitle">Krewire operates on an open core model: every line of code inside krewire/krewire is 100% open source (MIT). The ecosystem starts on the free tier — free forever — and climbs a four-rung ladder of pro, team, and enterprise.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- THE 4-RUNG TIER LADDER (SSOT: open-core.md) -->
      <div class="open-core-grid">
        <!-- Tier 1: free -->
        <div class="open-core-card">
          <div class="tier-top">
            <span class="tier-badge free" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_badge">Free Forever</span>
            <h3 class="tier-name font-mono" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_name">free</h3>
            <span class="tier-target" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_target">Students, UMKM, hobbyists, evaluation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="tier-desc" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_desc">The whole path from requirement to running product. A project built entirely on free modules builds, deploys, and operates with no license key, no seat count, no telemetry, and no expiry.</p>
          <ul class="tier-features">
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_f1">100% Open source (MIT License)</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_f2">Self-serve, no account or license key needed</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_f3">All core modules (kern, web, ui, tui, runtime, i18n, assets, cloud, testing, hub)</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tier-footer">
            <a href="#pathways" class="btn btn-outline w-full" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier1_cta">Get Started (Free) →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tier 2: pro -->
        <div class="open-core-card highlight-card">
          <div class="tier-top">
            <span class="tier-badge pro" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_badge">Planned Tier</span>
            <h3 class="tier-name font-mono" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_name">pro</h3>
            <span class="tier-target" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_target">Individual developers, freelancers, advanced products</span>
          </div>
          <p class="tier-desc" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_desc">Self-serve production reliability: distinguishes production-grade operational commitments, hardened security, managed secrets, and commercial sponsorship entitlements.</p>
          <ul class="tier-features">
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_f1">100% Open source (MIT License)</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_f2">Hardened security &amp; signed release pipeline</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_f3">Managed secrets &amp; KMS-backed credential rotation</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tier-footer">
            <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/krewire" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary w-full" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier2_cta">Sponsor on GitHub →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tier 3: team -->
        <div class="open-core-card">
          <div class="tier-top">
            <span class="tier-badge team" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_badge">Planned Tier</span>
            <h3 class="tier-name font-mono" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_name">team</h3>
            <span class="tier-target" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_target">Growing teams and agencies (multi-contributor)</span>
          </div>
          <p class="tier-desc" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_desc">Collaboration and fleet policy: shared configuration, team-wide policy, role separation across environments, and aggregate reporting.</p>
          <ul class="tier-features">
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_f1">100% Open source (MIT License)</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_f2">Team-wide policy &amp; role separation</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_f3">Fleet-level dashboards, cost &amp; usage visibility</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tier-footer">
            <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/krewire" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary w-full" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier3_cta">Sponsor on GitHub →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tier 4: enterprise -->
        <div class="open-core-card">
          <div class="tier-top">
            <span class="tier-badge enterprise" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_badge">Custom B2B</span>
            <h3 class="tier-name font-mono" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_name">enterprise</h3>
            <span class="tier-target" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_target">Organizations with procurement, compliance, or SLA needs</span>
          </div>
          <p class="tier-desc" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_desc">Deliberately not a self-serve product. Negotiated contract with compliance guarantees, named support contacts, immutable audit logging, and private registry support.</p>
          <ul class="tier-features">
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_f1">100% Open source core (MIT License)</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_f2">Immutable audit logs &amp; data retention enforcement</li>
            <li data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_f3">Defined availability SLA &amp; named support contact</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="tier-footer">
            <a href="mailto:sponsorship@krewire.com" class="btn btn-outline w-full" data-i18n="sponsorship.tier4_cta">Inquire for Enterprise B2B →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- SPONSORSHIP CHANNELS HUB -->
      <div class="sponsor-hub-box mt-8">
        <div class="sponsor-hub-inner">
          <div class="sponsor-hub-info">
            <h3 class="font-black text-lg mb-1" data-i18n="sponsorship.sponsor_box_title">Sponsoring the Krewire Collective</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted" data-i18n="sponsorship.sponsor_box_desc">Sponsorship fuels independent infrastructure, code signing attestations, and sustained open-source development. Choose your preferred channel to support:</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sponsor-hub-actions flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/krewire" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" data-i18n="sponsorship.sponsor_gh_btn">Sponsor via GitHub Sponsors 💖</a>
            <a href="mailto:sponsorship@krewire.com" class="btn btn-outline" data-i18n="sponsorship.sponsor_b2b_btn">Contact for Enterprise B2B Inquiry →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AI BOOST SYNERGY -->
  <section class="guild-section" id="boost">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="guild-card">
        <div class="guild-grid">
          <div class="guild-info">
            <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="guild.badge">Human + AI Synergy</div>
            <h2 data-i18n="guild.title">Collaborating with AI Boost</h2>
            <p class="guild-lead" data-i18n="guild.lead">Krewire pioneers the collaboration between human maintainers and autonomous AI agents. Our AI Boost framework operates with strict verification standards:</p>
            <ul class="guild-items">
              <li data-i18n-html="guild.item1_html"><b>Automated Architecture Audits:</b> AI agents check PRs against <code>KWF-*</code> specifications.</li>
              <li data-i18n-html="guild.item2_html"><b>Continuous Regression Hunting:</b> Agents synthesize edge cases and race condition checks.</li>
              <li data-i18n-html="guild.item3_html"><b>Transparent Pair Programming:</b> AI agents explain architectural decisions openly in discussions and PR comments.</li>
              <li data-i18n-html="guild.item4_html"><b>Human Governance:</b> Ultimate merging authority always remains in the hands of human collective maintainers.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="guild-ctas flex flex-wrap gap-3">
              <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/tree/main/templates/boost" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" data-i18n="guild.cta_repo">Explore AI Boost in Krewire →</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/orgs/krewire/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline" data-i18n="guild.cta_disc">Join Discussions</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="guild-triad">
            <div class="guild-box">
              <div class="guild-box-head">
                <span class="triad-icon">◈</span>
                <strong data-i18n="guild.triad_title">AI Boost Agent Triad</strong>
              </div>
              <div class="triad-roles">
                <div class="triad-role">
                  <div class="role-badge planner">Planner</div>
                  <strong data-i18n="guild.planner_title">Requirements &amp; SDD</strong>
                  <p data-i18n="guild.planner_desc">Translates feature ideas into formal specs and architectural blueprints.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="triad-role">
                  <div class="role-badge builder">Builder</div>
                  <strong data-i18n="guild.builder_title">Implementation &amp; Refactoring</strong>
                  <p data-i18n="guild.builder_desc">Generates clean Go implementations adhering to idiomatic patterns.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="triad-role">
                  <div class="role-badge auditor">Auditor</div>
                  <strong data-i18n="guild.auditor_title">Verification &amp; Quality Gates</strong>
                  <p data-i18n="guild.auditor_desc">Validates concurrency, zero data races, and performance benchmarks.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CALL TO ACTION -->
  <section class="final-cta" id="cta">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="cta-card">
        <div class="sub-badge" data-i18n="cta.badge">Join the Collective</div>
        <h2 data-i18n="cta.title">Ready to Shape the Future of Indonesian Tech?</h2>
        <p class="cta-lead" data-i18n="cta.lead">Whether you are writing your first Go pull request or sponsoring our developer community, you are laying the foundation for open-source self-reliance.</p>
        <div class="ctas flex flex-wrap gap-3 justify-center">
          <a href="https://github.com/krewire/krewire/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-i18n="cta.github">Explore Open Issues on GitHub →</a>
          <a href="#sponsorship" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg" data-i18n="cta.sponsor">Sponsor on GitHub 💖</a>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-meta" data-i18n="cta.meta">Proudly open source · MIT Licensed · Engineered with passion in Indonesia</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<style>
/* ==========================================================================
   KREWIRE COMMUNITY PORTAL STYLING
   Neo-brutalist, accessible, responsive
   ========================================================================== */

/* 1. HERO SECTION */
.hero {
  padding: 38px 0 28px;
  background: var(--bg);
  position: relative;
}
.hero-inner {
  max-width: 80rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 16px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 28px;
  align-items: center;
}
.hero-copy {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 16px;
}
.eyebrow {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  font-size: 11.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--primary-content);
  background: var(--primary);
  border: var(--pop-border-thin);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow-sm);
  padding: 3px 9px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  width: fit-content;
}
.hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(26px, 5vw, 44px);
  font-weight: 900;
  line-height: 1.15;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--fg);
}
.hero .lead {
  font-size: 14.5px;
  line-height: 1.65;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 580px;
}
.hero .meta {
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--muted);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

/* TERMINAL CARD */
.code-terminal-card {
  background: #0B1F3B;
  border: 2.5px solid var(--border);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow);
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  color: #FAF8F4;
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 12.5px;
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .code-terminal-card {
  border-color: #FAF8F4;
  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px var(--primary);
}
.code-terminal-bar {
  background: #112646;
  padding: 8px 12px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(250, 248, 244, 0.12);
}
.terminal-dots {
  display: flex;
  gap: 6px;
}
.term-dot {
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  display: inline-block;
}
.term-dot.red { background: #FF3B2E; }
.term-dot.yellow { background: #ffb703; }
.term-dot.green { background: #39D353; }
.term-title {
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #9ab0ce;
}
.code-terminal-body {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 6px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
.term-line {
  word-break: break-all;
}
.term-prompt {
  color: #39D353;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin-right: 6px;
}
.term-cmd {
  color: #FAF8F4;
  font-weight: 700;
}
.term-info {
  color: #00D1C1;
  font-size: 11.5px;
}
.term-success {
  color: #39D353;
  font-size: 11.5px;
  font-weight: 700;
}
.term-muted {
  color: #8fa2bc;
  font-size: 11px;
}

/* 2. TRUST BAR */
.trust {
  border-top: var(--pop-border);
  border-bottom: var(--pop-border);
  background: var(--bg-2);
  padding: 12px 16px;
}
.trust-inner {
  max-width: 80rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 12px;
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 700;
}
.trust-label {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--muted);
}
.trust-items {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.trust-item b {
  color: var(--primary-content);
  background: var(--primary);
  padding: 1px 6px;
  border-radius: 4px;
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .trust-item b {
  color: #0B1F3B;
  background: var(--primary);
}
.dot {
  color: var(--muted);
  opacity: 0.6;
}

/* SECTION COMMONS */
.section-inner {
  max-width: 80rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 16px;
}
.section-head {
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
}
.sub-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  background: var(--secondary);
  color: var(--secondary-content);
  padding: 3px 9px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  box-shadow: 1.5px 1.5px 0px var(--border);
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.section-head h2 {
  font-size: clamp(22px, 3.5vw, 32px);
  font-weight: 900;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  margin: 0 0 8px;
}
.section-head p {
  font-size: 14.5px;
  color: var(--muted);
  max-width: 680px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

/* 3. CONTRIBUTOR PRIVILEGES (BENEFITS) */
.benefits {
  padding: 42px 0 28px;
}
.benefit-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 16px;
}
.benefit-card {
  background: var(--bg);
  border: var(--pop-border);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 20px 18px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 12px;
  transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
}
.benefit-card:hover {
  transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow-lg);
}
.benefit-card.highlight-card {
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border-color: var(--primary);
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] .benefit-card.highlight-card {
  border-color: var(--primary);
  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px var(--primary);
}
.benefit-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  background: var(--primary);
  color: var(--primary-content);
  padding: 2px 7px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  width: fit-content;
}
.benefit-card h3 {
  font-size: 17px;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin: 0;
}
.benefit-card p {
  font-size: 13.5px;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
.benefit-list {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.benefit-list li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 8px;
}
.benefit-list li::before {
  content: "✓";
  color: var(--primary);
  font-weight: 900;
}
.meritocracy-callout {
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: var(--pop-border);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow-sm);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 16px 20px;
}
.meritocracy-inner {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 16px;
}
.meritocracy-icon {
  font-size: 26px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.meritocracy-body strong {
  display: block;
  font-size: 14.5px;
  margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.meritocracy-body p {
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* 4. CODEBASE MATRIX & REPOSITORIES */
.repos-nav {
  padding: 42px 0 28px;
}
.fast-setup-box {
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: var(--pop-border);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 18px 20px;
}
.fast-setup-header {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.fast-setup-title {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 900;
}
.fast-setup-badge {
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  background: var(--primary);
  color: var(--primary-content);
  padding: 2px 7px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
}
.fast-setup-desc {
  font-size: 13.5px;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0 0 12px;
}
.terminal-cmd-bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 10px;
  background: #0B1F3B;
  color: #FAF8F4;
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 8px 12px;
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 12.5px;
}
.terminal-cmd-bar code {
  overflow-x: auto;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.btn-copy {
  background: var(--primary);
  color: var(--primary-content);
  border: 1.5px solid #0B1F3B;
  box-shadow: 1.5px 1.5px 0px #0B1F3B;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 4px 10px;
  font-size: 11.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  cursor: pointer;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  transition: all 0.12s ease;
}
.btn-copy:hover {
  transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
  box-shadow: 2.5px 2.5px 0px #0B1F3B;
}
.btn-copy.copied {
  background: var(--secondary);
}
.fast-setup-meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font-size: 11.5px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-weight: 700;
  margin-top: 10px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

/* FILTERS */
.nav-filters {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.filter-label {
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--muted);
}
.filter-pills {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.filter-pill {
  border: var(--pop-border-thin);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow-sm);
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 800;
  padding: 5px 12px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.12s ease;
}
.filter-pill:hover {
  transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
  box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-2);
}
.filter-pill.is-active {
  background: var(--primary);
  color: var(--primary-content);
}

/* REPOSITORIES GRID */
.repo-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 16px;
}
.repo-card {
  background: var(--bg);
  border: var(--pop-border);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  padding: 20px 18px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 12px;
  transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
}
.repo-card:hover {
  transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
  box-shadow: var(--pop-shadow-lg);
}
.repo-meta-top {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.repo-tag {
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 2px 7px;
  border-radius: 5px;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
}
.repo-tag.core { background: var(--primary); color: var(--primary-content); }
.repo-tag.tool { background: var(--secondary); color: var(--secondary-content); }
.repo-tag.site { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
.repo-tag.docs { background: #ffb703; color: #0B1F3B; }
.repo-lang {
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--muted);
}
.repo-title {
  font-size: 18px;
  font-weight: 900;
  margin: 0;
}
.repo-title a:hover {
  color: var(--primary);
}
.repo-track-name {
  font-size: 12.5px;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--muted);
}
.repo-match {
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--muted);
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 0;
}
.repo-pkgs {
  margin-top: 8px;
}
.pkgs-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  color: var(--muted);
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 5px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}
.pkgs-chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 5px;
}
.pkg-chip {
  font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
